{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Recipe",
  "recipeCuisine": "Japan",
  "name": "Roast Beef",
  "text": "Roast Beef\n\nPreparation time:\n\nCooking time:\n\nYield: 4\n\nIngredients\n\n300 g silverside (at room temperature),\n\nsalt and coarsely ground pepper,\n\n200 ml dashi stock,\n\n50 ml soy sauce,\n\n40 ml mirin.\n\nGarnish\n\n4 shiso leaves,\n\ncress,\n\n¼ onion (thinly sliced).\n\nPreparation\n\n1. In a small deep saucepan, combine the dashi stock, soy sauce, and mirin.\n\n2. Bring the mixture to the boil, then remove from the heat.\n\n3. Season the beef with salt and pepper.\n\n4. Brown the beef on all sides in a hot frying pan with vegetable oil.\n\n5. Add the meat to the liquid, bring to the boil, then reduce the heat to a very gentle simmer.\n\n6. Cook for 15 minutes, ladling the sauce over the meat, and turning occasionally.\n\n7. Soak the thinly sliced onion in a bowl of ice water for 5 minutes, then dry with a paper towel.\n\n8. Put the onion in the center of a long thin plate, with the shiso leaves at either end.\n\n9. Slice the beef very thinly. and place over the onion.\n\n10. Top with cress.\n\n11. Serve the stock as a sauce, in a bowl.",
  "recipeYield": "4",
